// expect-error: `Zeroable` is an `unsafe trait`: the impl promises what the compiler cannot check; write `unsafe impl Zeroable for i32`
// expect-error: `Plain` is not an auto trait or an `unsafe trait` - `unsafe impl` is only for `Send`, `Sync` and `unsafe trait`s, `impl !Trait` only for `Send` / `Sync`; write `impl Plain for i32`
// expect-error: `impl !Zeroable`: `impl !Trait` is only for the auto traits `Send` / `Sync`; remove it (a type without `unsafe impl Zeroable` does not have it)
// expect-error: `Pod` is an `unsafe trait`: the impl promises what the compiler cannot check; write `unsafe impl Pod for Pair`

// An `unsafe trait` takes only `unsafe impl`; a safe trait never does.
use rok::bare::mem::Pod;

unsafe trait Zeroable {}
trait Plain {}

impl Zeroable for i32 {}
unsafe impl Plain for i32 {}
impl !Zeroable for u8 {}

#[repr(C)]
struct Pair { a: u32; b: u32; }

impl Pod for Pair {}

fn main() {}

